# {{PROJECT_NAME}} agent guide

Read `publishing.project.json` before changing content, accounts, assets, resources, or publication behavior.

- Keep `{{PROFILE}}` as the starting profile and document every intentional overlay.
- Preserve the project's canonical content representation; use adapters at system boundaries.
- Pin the current revision before edits. Never overwrite a conflicting revision silently.
- Choose `direct` edits only when both policy and user intent allow them; otherwise create a proposal.
- Validate content, links, assets, resources, and permissions before publication.
- Show a preview or diff before publish, rollback, quarantine, or role changes.
- Record why generated files or profile defaults were changed locally.
- Convert recurring local changes into an upstream Issue or PR when they are broadly reusable.

Run `epk doctor .` after changing the project manifest or managed template files.
